=== DESIGN ===
Codegen binary cmd/protogen-tesla/ produces three files in internal/tesla/protomodel/:
  signal_metadata_gen.go  - Field enum (consts + ParseField + Name + String) + SignalMeta struct + SignalMetaByField map
  enum_parsers_gen.go     - Every other named enum: type + const block + String() + ParseXxx(s string) (Xxx, error)
  datum_decoder_gen.go    - Compound message types (LocationValue, Doors, TireLocation, Time) + Value (oneof) + Datum + Payload + DecodeValue (honors v.Invalid via ErrInvalidDatum)
Architecture:
  parser.go - Hand-rolled proto3 lexer (tokenize) + recursive-descent parser (parseFile/parseEnum/parseMessage/parseOneof/parseField). Skips top-level syntax/package/import/option statements. Sorts everything (enums, values, fields, oneof variants) for deterministic output.
  emit.go   - Three text/template templates + classifier table (260 explicit cases canonicalized from fleet-telemetry-audit coverage.json). Output piped through go/format.Source for gofmt-stable bytes. classify(name) returns (fieldClass, found bool) so the test can detect fall-through.
  main.go   - CLI flags --proto, --out, --package with sensible defaults. Calls ParseProtoFile + Emit.
Determinism guarantees:
  * canonicalize() sorts ProtoFile in stable order before emission.
  * Templates iterate over sorted slices (never maps).
  * go/format.Source is deterministic for any well-formed Go input.
  * No time.Now(), no random, no map iteration in the rendering path.

